# DURABLE REPRO PROCEDURE for the SH-lowerer stage-2 double-free.
#
# R37 (2026-08-08) filed as "triggered by the formatter's bulk
# canonicalization".
#
# R39 Track A Phase 1 (2026-08-09) claimed the mechanism was corrected —
# "the fmt sweep is not the trigger; reproduces on a clean tree at
# stage-3 without ANY fmt sweep". Phase 2 (2026-08-09) RETRACTS that
# claim: verified against current HEAD (`0ed1c2315`),
# `self_host_bootstrap_fixed_point` PASSES cleanly WITHOUT the fmt sweep
# (stage-2.c == stage-3.c, converges at K=2). Phase 1's raw --lir-c-
# only-cc reproducer skipped the runtime preamble splice; that shape
# never was a valid clean-tree crash. The fmt sweep IS the trigger.
#
# ── Phase 2 refined diagnosis (fmt sweep required to reproduce):
#
# With the fmt sweep applied on the non-SH corpus (as
# `sh_bootstrap_stage2_double_free_after_fmt_sweep` does), the bootstrap
# reproduces reliably:
#
#   stage-0 (Rust-compiled SH lowerer) → stage-1.c CORRECT (no extra
#     unconditional frees at consuming-mutator call sites)
#   stage-1 (SH-compiled from stage-1.c) → stage-2.c BUGGY: emits
#     UNCONDITIONAL `gorget_string_free(&slot)` after `gorget_map_put`
#     for values that were moved into the map (drop_elab decided
#     INITIALIZED instead of UNINITIALIZED for the moved slot)
#   stage-2 (SH-compiled from stage-2.c) → CRASHES with exit 134
#     `free(): double free detected in tcache 2`
#
# ── ASan on the crashing stage-2 binary (aarch64, 2026-08-09):
#
#   AddressSanitizer: heap-use-after-free
#   READ at __gorget_hash_str_len ← __gorget_str_key_hash ←
#         __gorget_map_dense_grow ← gorget_map_put ←
#         loader___load_imports (self_host_stage2.c:461222)
#   freed by gorget_string_free ← loader___load_imports (:461226)
#   allocated by gorget_string_clone_to_owned ← loader___load_imports
#         (:461215)
#
# The exact bad C in stage-2 at the crash site:
#
#   __v112 = gorget_string_clone_to_owned(__v111);   /* alloc */
#   __s53 = __v112;
#   gorget_map_put(__v115, &__s53, &__s54);          /* moves __s53 in */
#   __v119 = &__s53;
#   gorget_string_free(__v119);                      /* BUG: unconditional */
#
# Loop iteration N+1's `gorget_map_put` hashes existing keys → reads the
# already-freed data from iteration N → UAF.
#
# The corresponding SH source at `loader.gg:663` is:
#   `loaded.put(imp.module_path.clone(), true)`
#
# ── Root-cause chain (write site per Core #1):
#
# stage-1's `drop_elab.gg::elaborate_block` decides INITIALIZED for the
# moved-into-map slot where stage-0 correctly decides UNINITIALIZED
# (moved, delete drop). The chain that should produce UNINITIALIZED:
#   1. `op_consume` / `decide_operand_at_consuming_arg`
#      (lower.gg:2603+, :2779+) picks OpMove for the moved arg
#   2. `wire_liveness_into_modes` (lower_liveness.gg:807-812) emits
#      `GIMoveZero(lid)` after the moving inst
#   3. lir_lower translates `GIMoveZero` → `IMoveSlot`
#   4. `drop_elab::apply_inst_effect` sees `IMoveSlot` → marks slot
#      Uninitialized → strip guard, delete drop
#
# Stage-1's algorithm — implementing THIS SAME chain — produces a wrong
# result at ONE step. Since ASan on stage-1 binary finds NO memory
# errors during its execution, the bug is NOT a UB in stage-1's
# runtime — it's a codegen bug: SH's own compilation of some SH lowerer
# construct produces C whose runtime SEMANTICS differ from Rust's C for
# the same source construct, without introducing UB.
#
# ── Diff stats (stage-1.c vs stage-2.c, post-fmt-sweep):
#
#   +741 extra `gorget_{string,array,map,set}_free` unconditional calls
#   -431 fewer bool drop-flag storage decls (`bool __coal*` / `bool __s*`)
#   +2 empty `struct __gg_R` / `struct __gg_W` (unmonomorphized W/R type
#      params from `write_all[W]`/`reader_drain[R]` in `lib/std/io.gg` —
#      the `is_generic_placeholder_name` filter at lir_lower.gg:600 lists
#      T/E/K/V/U but NOT R/W). Independent minor gap; not the crash.
#
# ── Phase 2 bisection outcome (partial):
#
# Applying fmt to `lib/std/io.gg` ALONE does NOT trigger the crash
# (bootstrap converges; only the R/W empty-struct additions appear).
# Some OTHER file(s) in the 1924 fmt-changed files contribute. Full
# bisection: ~11 rounds × 7min bootstrap = ~1.3h + overhead.
#
# ── Phase 2b bisection outcome (2026-08-09, narrowed to ONE file):
#
# The trigger narrows to `compiler/data/resources.gg`.  Verified:
#   * reset all + fmt EVERY file EXCEPT `compiler/data/*.gg` → bootstrap
#     CONVERGES cleanly (stage-2 exit 0, stage-2.c == stage-3.c).
#   * reset all + fmt ONLY `compiler/data/resources.gg` (leave every
#     other file untouched) → bootstrap CRASHES with the same
#     `free(): double free detected in tcache 2` at stage-2.
#
# `compiler/data/resources.gg` is a data-only module describing the
# runtime resource table (~139 `ResourceEntry(...)` literals).  The
# SH driver reads it at runtime via project-root fallback (`from
# compiler.data.resources import ...` in the loader.gg / lower_*.gg
# family), so its on-disk contents are load-bearing for both the Rust
# build of `driver_post_sweep` (used as stage-0) AND the SH-emitted
# stage-N drivers.
#
# ── Phase 2b diagnostic — where SH-emit diverges on the fmt'd file:
#
# Comparing `__gg_static_init_RESOURCES` in `stage_1.c` (Rust-emit of
# fmt'd resources.gg, correct) vs `stage_2.c` (SH-emit compiled from
# stage_1.c, buggy) shows the SH-emit is MISSING two stack slots per
# `ResourceEntry`:
#
#   Rust-emit (per iteration, N=139):
#     __gg_ResourceMetadata __s27 = {0};   /* temp for the nested ctor */
#     __gg_ResourceEntry    __s28 = {0};   /* temp for the outer ctor  */
#     ...
#   SH-emit: those two slot decls are absent — the ctor result is
#     stored directly into the RESOURCES vector element without an
#     intermediate slot.
#
# The single-line vs multi-line ctor shape in the source drives this:
# fmt reformats `ResourceEntry([...], ResourceMetadata("Gorget...", 32,
# LtStructBase(), Some("gorget_string_free"), ...))` from a compact
# one-per-line form into a "one argument per line with trailing comma"
# form.  Both parse to the same AST in Rust gg (verified — Rust builds
# stage-0/driver_post_sweep and it works), but the SH lowerer takes a
# DIFFERENT PATH for the multi-line ctor shape and elides the
# ResourceMetadata / ResourceEntry temp slots.  That elision breaks
# drop_elab's tracking downstream — hundreds of `map_put` sites end
# up with spurious `gorget_string_free(&slot)` calls in stage-2.c
# (~118 spurious put+free-within-5-lines patterns in `loader___load_
# imports` alone vs 34 in the Rust reference and 9 in stage-1.c).
#
# Cross-checks that let us stop here (not the trigger):
#   * `blocking` / `noreturn` extern qualifiers stripped by fmt — real
#     formatter bug (`src/formatter/mod.rs::format_qualifiers` at
#     :573-586 lists `is_async/is_const/is_static/is_unsafe` but not
#     `is_blocking/is_noreturn`), but reset-lib alone does NOT stop
#     the crash and only compiler/data/resources.gg contributes.
#   * Import re-ordering to alphabetic within `from X import ...`:
#     changes the file but does not by itself flip stage-2 to the
#     double-free (partial isolated test showed a HANG at stage-2's
#     driver.gg self-compile — a distinct failure signature, not the
#     double-free class).
#   * Comment removal from Vector literals (fmt DROPS inline `#…`
#     comments between elements of `RESOURCES = [ … ]` in
#     resources.gg): semantically neutral, but again a formatter
#     preservation gap worth its own filing.
#
# ── Phase 2c bisection outcome (2026-08-09, Path C partial + narrowing continued):
#
# Post-rebase (onto `1664da711`, which includes the extern-qualifier
# chip `4deee6e56` + snag #2 trailing-comment fix `f4b98a681`), A1
# STILL REPRODUCES with the same signature (`stage-2 exit 134`,
# `free(): double free detected in tcache 2`). Neither the
# extern-qualifier fix nor the trailing-comment attachment fix
# incidentally repaired A1 — the SH-side ctor lowering divergence is
# independent of those two formatter defects. (Core #5 re-verified.)
#
# Path C step 1 executed — refutes the "single-ctor-shape flip"
# hypothesis: rewriting ONE `ResourceEntry(...)` literal in HEAD's
# resources.gg from single-line into fmt's multi-line "one arg per
# line with trailing comma" shape (nothing else changed) → bootstrap
# CONVERGES cleanly (stage-2 exit 0). So the SH lowering divergence
# is NOT triggered by a single ctor-shape change; it accumulates.
#
# Additional isolated Path A slices tested (all against a clean
# starting tree, `driver_pre_sweep`-equivalent post-rebase):
#   * fmt applied EXCEPT reverting the 8 import re-orderings in
#     resources.gg → still CRASHES with the double-free (imports are
#     NOT the trigger; some other fmt-change is).
#   * import re-ordering ALONE (no other fmt changes to resources.gg)
#     → CONVERGES. Imports alone are not enough to flip either.
#   * fmt applied then all trailing commas removed programmatically
#     (`,\n[ ]*)` → `\n[ ]*)`) → SH-stage-2 HUNG (~4 min producing
#     4KB, killed) — a distinct "hang" symptom from the double-free,
#     but still a self-hosting divergence.
#   * fmt applied ONLY inside the RESOURCES section (kept HEAD's form
#     for RUNTIME_FNS/BUILTIN_METHOD_MUTATES/etc.) → SH-stage-2
#     HUNG (same 4KB pattern), killed at 5 min.
#
# The pattern that emerges: multiple fmt-shape changes to
# `compiler/data/resources.gg` accumulate into a self-hosting
# divergence, but the exact minimal trigger set is NOT a single
# structural change (import reorder alone / trailing commas alone /
# one ctor multi-line alone). The trigger appears CUMULATIVE across
# multiple ctor-shape rewrites AND/OR interacts with an accumulated
# whitespace/comment structure. Further narrowing requires either:
#   (a) A binary-search over lines of the fmt output (halve until
#       flip observed), which is slow because every step requires a
#       full 8-10 min bootstrap; OR
#   (b) Instrument the SH lowerer's Call/Ctor path to log the
#       "temp slot emit vs elide" decision per-ctor and diff the
#       decisions between fmt'd and clean resources.gg. This is
#       more principled but requires editing `lower_expr.gg` /
#       `lower.gg` + a self-host rebuild between each iteration.
#
# ── PROGRESS STOPPED HERE per stop-condition "Path C step 3 (branch
# localization) > 4h without narrowing" (session used ~7h — Phase
# 2b bisection ~5h + Phase 2c Path C narrowing ~2h). Owner-visible
# rescope proposal:
#
#   The A1 fix is more expensive than the initial estimate suggested,
#   because the trigger is CUMULATIVE not single-shape and the SH
#   Call/Ctor lowering has ~10K LOC of arm-branching (`lower_call`
#   alone starts at `lower_expr.gg:7947` and spans ~1000+ lines).
#   Recommended next-round shape:
#     Phase 2d — Instrument the SH lowerer's temp-slot-elision path
#     (add debug prints to the exact write site in `lower_expr.gg`
#     that decides `add_local` vs direct-store for ctor results in
#     Vector element positions), run once with clean and once with
#     fmt'd resources.gg, diff the per-ctor decision log. That
#     yields a minimal SH source pair that triggers the divergence
#     on a single ctor site (Path C step 1's single-ctor probe was
#     too coarse — the difference likely lies in the INTERACTION
#     between adjacent ctors' slot IDs, not in a single ctor).
#     Budget: ~1-2 days.
#     Then Phase 2e — Fix at the write site (Core #1) with a
#     regression fixture that exercises the multi-ctor-inside-Vector
#     shape. Estimated ~1 day.
#
# The R40+ fix paths above remain valid; Path C is REFINED not
# refuted (single ctor is too coarse; must instrument to see the
# per-ctor decision).
#
# ── R40+ fix paths (updated by Phase 2b; Path C REFINED by Phase 2c):
#
# Path C (highest signal, REFINED) — hypothesis-test the ctor-shape
# divergence via instrumentation, not via source-shape rewriting:
#   1. Add debug prints to the SH lowerer at the write site in
#      `lower_expr.gg` where ctor calls decide temp-slot allocation
#      (grep for `add_local` calls with an owning-typed result
#      inside `lower_call` / the ctor handlers). Log per-ctor
#      "TEMP_SLOT=yes/no" plus the source line.
#   2. Rebuild driver + run once against clean resources.gg and once
#      against fmt'd resources.gg. Diff the two logs.
#   3. Isolate the FIRST ctor whose decision flips. That ctor's
#      shape difference is the minimal trigger.
#   4. Fix at the write site: the branch should emit consistently
#      regardless of source shape.
#
# Old Path C step 1 (Phase 2b) — REFUTED by Phase 2c:
# manually rewriting ONE `ResourceEntry(...)` literal alone does
# NOT flip stage-2 (bootstrap converges). Trigger is CUMULATIVE.
#
# (rest of R40 fix paths retained below — Path A/B still valid
# alternatives; Path C above is the recommended next move.)
#
# — Original Path C (Phase 2b) description for context:
#   1. Manually restructure ONE `ResourceEntry(...)` literal in
#      HEAD's resources.gg from single-line into fmt's multi-line
#      shape (nothing else — no import reorder, no comment removal).
#   2. Rebuild driver + rerun `self_host_bootstrap_fixed_point`.
#   3. If it crashes: the trigger is the multi-line ctor lowering —
#      dig into `lower.gg` / `lower_expr.gg`'s handling of Call and
#      Ctor expressions to find the shape-dependent branch that
#      elides the ResourceMetadata/ResourceEntry temp slots.
#   4. If it does NOT crash: the trigger is CUMULATIVE — needs N
#      such rewrites before flipping — instrumentation via a small
#      per-ctor rewrite script + N-vs-outcome sweep.
# Path A — fmt bisection (superseded — already narrowed to one file).
# Path B — emitter diff at drop_elab/lower_liveness (Phase 2b ruled
#   in as INSUFFICIENT: the drift is UPSTREAM, in ctor lowering, so
#   drop_elab reads mis-initialized dataflow state; Core #1 rule
#   applies — fix at the write site in lower_expr, not read site in
#   drop_elab).
#
# ── R40 fix paths (retained from Phase 2 for reference):
#
# Path A — fmt bisection: narrow to specific file/canonicalization, then
#   grep the file for the SH construct that miscompiles.
# Path B — emitter diff: compare
#   `tests/fixtures/self_host_lowerer/driver.c` (Rust-emit of SH source)
#   vs freshly-generated stage-1.c (SH-emit) at
#   `drop_elab___elaborate_block`, `drop_elab___apply_inst_effect`,
#   `lower_liveness___wire_one_operand`, and
#   `lower_liveness___rewrite_inst_modes`. Find the specific
#   instruction sequence that differs. Trace back to SH source. Fix at
#   the write site.
#
# ── R40 reproducer (regeneration, per the wrapper test's shape — NOT
# the raw --lir-c-only shape Phase 1 originally used, which lacks the
# runtime preamble and won't cc):
#
#   1. `cargo build --release --bin gg`
#   2. Apply fmt to non-SH corpus (see the wrapper test at
#      `tests/integration.rs::sh_bootstrap_stage2_double_free_after_fmt_sweep`
#      for the exact enumeration; script equivalent:
#      `find tests/fixtures lib examples demo spectests compiler/data \
#            -name '*.gg' -not -path '*/self_host_*/*' | \
#         xargs -P 8 -I{} ./target/release/gg fmt --in-place {}`)
#   3. `rm -f tests/fixtures/self_host_lowerer/driver{,.c}`
#   4. `GG_BUILD_TIMEOUT_SECS=900 GG_TEST_TIMEOUT_SECS=600 \
#         cargo test --test integration --release \
#         self_host_bootstrap_fixed_point`
#      → REPRODUCES: `stage-2 binary failed: stderr=free(): double free
#        detected in tcache 2` (~8-10 min from clean cache).
#   5. To get an ASan trace: cc `/tmp/self_host_stage2.c` with
#      `-fsanitize=address -O0 -w -g` and run it against
#      `tests/fixtures/self_host_lowerer/driver.gg lib --lir-c`.
#
# ── Original filing framing (R37, superseded but preserved):
# Orthogonal to D27 — reproduces against the retired `!` glyph too, so
# the trigger is the FORMATTER'S BULK CANONICALIZATION, not the D27
# sigil swap. (R39 Track A refines: the fmt sweep is not even the
# trigger; the sweep just accelerates a pre-existing non-convergence.)
#
# The trigger is INTRINSICALLY PROCEDURAL — no single `.gg` input
# reproduces it in isolation. The double-free surfaces only after
# `gg fmt --in-place` sweeps a large fraction of the corpus and the
# resulting reformatted tree is bootstrapped via
# `self_host_bootstrap_fixed_point`. That means this file is the
# REPRO'S DOCUMENTATION, not a compileable input. The actual wrapper
# lives at `tests/integration.rs::sh_bootstrap_stage2_double_free_after_fmt_sweep`
# (`#[ignore]`d — asserts the CORRECT / intended behavior: the sweep
# followed by `self_host_bootstrap_fixed_point` succeeds).
#
# Un-ignore + promote out of `known_gaps/` when the SH-lowerer defect is
# diagnosed and fixed.
#
# ── The procedure that reproduces the failure (executor-verified twice
# during R37, 2026-08-08):
#
#   1. Start from a clean tree at HEAD.
#   2. `cargo build --release --bin gg`
#   3. Run `gg fmt --in-place` recursively over the D27 sweep corpora
#      (or over just the non-SH subset — either triggers the failure):
#        - Full sweep: `scripts/fmt_sweep_smoke.sh --apply`  (2,847 files
#          touched, 2,007 changed)
#        - Non-SH-only:  `find tests/fixtures lib examples demo spectests
#          compiler/data -name '*.gg' -not -path '*/self_host_*/*' -exec
#          ./target/release/gg fmt --in-place {} \;`
#          (2,754 files, 1,915 changed)
#   4. Delete any cached driver binaries:
#        `rm -f tests/fixtures/self_host_lowerer/driver
#               tests/fixtures/self_host_lowerer/driver.c`
#   5. `GG_BUILD_TIMEOUT_SECS=900 GG_TEST_TIMEOUT_SECS=600 cargo test
#          --test integration --release self_host_bootstrap_fixed_point`
#   6. OBSERVED failure at stage 2:
#        thread 'self_host_bootstrap_fixed_point' panicked at
#          tests/integration.rs:22030:9:
#        stage-2 binary failed: stderr=free(): double free detected in tcache 2
#      The stage-0 driver builds and runs. Stage-1.c is emitted. The
#      stage-2 driver binary (built from stage-1.c) CRASHES when it runs
#      to produce stage-2.c. Stage-1 vs stage-2 comparison never happens.
#
# ── The bulk canonicalization the sweep performs (any one of these,
# combined at scale, is capable of tripping the SH-lowerer defect):
#
#   - import re-sort (alphabetical) + one-line-per-import expansion
#   - blank-line normalization (blank line between const decls,
#     between top-level items)
#   - empty-variant / empty-tuple-pattern paren-drop
#     (`case TkPlus():` -> `case TkPlus:`)
#   - kwarg spacing (`alloc=pool` -> `alloc = pool`)
#   - comment repositioning (comments before an `extern` statement can
#     get demoted out of an `equip` block to the outer scope)
#   - the D27 sigil swap (`!name` -> `^name`) itself is NOT the trigger:
#     confirmed by running the sweep on non-SH corpora only, which still
#     triggers the double-free even though SH fixtures keep `!` (parser
#     accept-both).
#
# ── This defect is a HARD blocker for the D27 Phase 2 in-place sweep.
# R37 shipped the emit swap + empty-body chip + arm-count + shrink-only
# lints without the sweep; users who want to migrate can run
# `gg fmt --in-place file.gg` on ONE file at a time (small-N appears
# safe — the SH lowerer only trips at scale). The full sweep waits on
# the SH-lowerer diagnosis.

# Sentinel body — this file's real content is the header procedure. Keep
# a trivial `main` so if someone accidentally routes `gg check` through
# it, they get a green result and a comment-pointer to the wrapper test.
int main():
    print("known_gap: see header comment + tests/integration.rs::sh_bootstrap_stage2_double_free_after_fmt_sweep")
    return 0
